      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "This project focused on increasing compliance, in a large family practice group, with quality indicators for the management of asthma. The objective was to determine if use of a flow sheet incorporating the Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA) guidelines could improve compliance with those guidelines if the flow sheet was placed in patients' medical records."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "After review and selection of 14 clinical quality indicators, physicians in the practice implemented a flow sheet as an intervention. These flow sheets were inserted into the records of 122 randomly selected patients with asthma. Medical records were reviewed before the flow sheets were placed in the records, and again approximately 6 months later, to determine if there was a change in compliance with the quality indicators."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Improvement of documentation was demonstrated in 13 of the 14 quality indicators."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The results indicate that compliance with asthma management quality indicators can improve with the use of a flow sheet."
        }
      ]},
